.TH @PROG@ 1 "@PROJECT_YEAR@" "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@PROG@, @COLON@ \- create zip archives using colon-path member names
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @COLON@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I zipfile
.I path
\&...
.br
.B @PROG@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @PROG@
is a colon-path wrapper around
.BR zip (1).
Sources given as
.B BASE:LEAF
are stored in the archive under
.I LEAF
(not under the full physical path
.BR BASE/LEAF ).
.PP
See
.BR colon-path (7).
.PP
The wrapper stages leaf names (via symlinks) and runs
.B zip \-r
from that staging directory unless
.B \-r
was already supplied.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B @COLON@ a.zip a/b:c/d/e
Creates
.B a.zip
whose members are rooted at
.B c/d/e/
(from physical tree
.BR a/b/c/d/e ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show wrapper help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-colon\-dry\-run
Show the planned
.B zip
invocation without executing it.
.PP
Other options are passed through to
.BR zip (1).
See the original manual for the complete option set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zip (1),
.BR colon-unzip (1),
.BR colon-path (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by @PROJECT_AUTHOR@ <@PROJECT_EMAIL@>.
